WEBVTT

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:02.664
Every business has one.

00:00:03.209 --> 00:00:05.590
The process nobody owns.

00:00:05.996 --> 00:00:08.608
It's done by hand because it's always

00:00:08.655 --> 00:00:09.874
been done by hand.

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:13.426
It takes two hours, it happens forty

00:00:13.496 --> 00:00:16.166
times a month, and everyone's too busy

00:00:16.236 --> 00:00:17.652
running it to fix it.

00:00:18.395 --> 00:00:20.381
You don't need advice about it.

00:00:21.008 --> 00:00:23.573
You need someone to come in and

00:00:23.701 --> 00:00:24.734
change it.

00:00:25.784 --> 00:00:28.745
That's what forward-deployed means, and it's the

00:00:28.803 --> 00:00:30.544
whole of how we work.

00:00:31.624 --> 00:00:34.410
We don't send a proposal and disappear.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.567
Our engineers embed in your business, work

00:00:38.625 --> 00:00:41.144
in your systems, learn how it actually

00:00:41.202 --> 00:00:44.348
runs, and automate it from the inside.

00:00:45.126 --> 00:00:46.659
The people who scope it are the

00:00:46.705 --> 00:00:47.796
people who build it.

00:00:48.435 --> 00:00:52.464
No pitch team, no handoff, no bench.

00:00:53.102 --> 00:00:56.574
Working software in weeks, not quarters.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.482
Two of our engineers sat inside a

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:02.744
training company and took student registration apart.

00:01:03.533 --> 00:01:06.134
It took two hours per student, every

00:01:06.239 --> 00:01:08.096
intake, by hand.

00:01:08.677 --> 00:01:09.594
They rebuilt it.

00:01:10.279 --> 00:01:10.999
Two minutes.

00:01:11.684 --> 00:01:15.643
Sixty times faster, and about thirty-nine staff

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:18.302
hours back on every twenty-student cohort.

00:01:18.708 --> 00:01:20.426
Nobody wrote a report about it.

00:01:20.775 --> 00:01:22.609
They just fixed it.

00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:25.052
And when what you need is software,

00:01:25.331 --> 00:01:28.199
we build that too, properly, for production.

00:01:28.802 --> 00:01:30.428
SeatStep is ours.

00:01:31.031 --> 00:01:34.271
iOS and Android, turn-by-turn from the turnstile

00:01:34.305 --> 00:01:36.871
to your seat, a live concourse map,

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:39.878
AR wayfinding for venues too loud and

00:01:39.925 --> 00:01:41.388
too crowded to think in.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:46.299
Web, mobile, data pipelines, dashboards,

00:01:46.368 --> 00:01:48.818
AI that does a real job.

00:01:49.456 --> 00:01:52.638
Same team, same model.

00:01:53.688 --> 00:01:56.149
The embedded model usually costs what a

00:01:56.242 --> 00:01:57.891
Fortune 500 pays.

00:01:58.471 --> 00:02:01.351
We built ours for small and mid-size

00:02:01.397 --> 00:02:04.334
businesses, because that's where the work actually

00:02:04.404 --> 00:02:05.147
gets done.

00:02:05.728 --> 00:02:08.351
And you own everything after.

00:02:08.851 --> 00:02:12.287
The code, the platform, the documentation,

00:02:12.461 --> 00:02:14.771
and the ability to run it without

00:02:14.853 --> 00:02:15.271
us.

00:02:15.677 --> 00:02:17.778
We plan the exit from day one.

00:02:18.185 --> 00:02:21.134
Dependency is a bug, not a business

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:21.703
model.

00:02:21.888 --> 00:02:23.816
Twenty minutes, and we'll tell you what

00:02:23.874 --> 00:02:25.592
we'd automate first.
